    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1958184463881347573",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1958184463881347573",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1958184463881347573",
      "text": "[4:06PM] #Apapa_Ajegunle #TrafficUpdate \n\nVehicular movement from Ojo Road and Otto Wharf remains smooth with fast traffic flow. The same applies to movement from Ajeromi Ifelodun through Baale Street to Boundary Bus Stop, where traffic is also moving freely. However, activity around Boundary Roundabout is relatively slow due to ongoing commercial and market activities in the area.\n\nFrom Boundary towards the Arrakan Military Cantonment, traffic is steady and without delays. At Marine Beach Bus Stop, inward Ijora, vehicles are moving at a fast pace, while traffic from Ijora Oloopa through the High Bridge to Total and Area B is also flowing freely on both lanes. Outward traffic from Apapa, covering Point Road through Marine Bridge to Iganmu, is equally smooth and without obstruction.\n\nThere are no impediments reported at the moment, and our officers are stationed at the major choke points, effectively managing movement and ensuring order.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
